---
import './figures.css';
---
<figure class="cl-figure" aria-labelledby="row-homes-title">
  <figcaption id="row-homes-title"><span class="cl-number">Figure 2</span> One table, two row homes</figcaption>
  <div class="cl-panel">
    <p class="cl-label">REGIONAL BY ROW · crdb_region prefixes every index</p>
    <div class="cl-three">
      <div class="cl-region"><strong>North</strong><div class="cl-card"><b>orders · primary</b><span>North / 101</span><span>North / 103</span></div><div class="cl-card"><b>orders_history</b><span>North / 1 / 20 Oct / 103</span><span>North / 1 / 12 Oct / 101</span></div><div class="cl-card"><b>Matching order lines</b><span>101 / 1, 101 / 2</span><span>103 / 1, 103 / 2</span><span class="cl-small">Explicitly assigned North</span></div></div>
      <div class="cl-region"><strong>West</strong><div class="cl-card"><b>orders · primary</b><span>West / 102</span></div><div class="cl-card"><b>orders_history</b><span>West / 2 / 14 Oct / 102</span></div><div class="cl-card"><b>Matching order line</b><span>102 / 1</span><span class="cl-small">Explicitly assigned West</span></div></div>
      <div class="cl-region"><strong>East</strong><div class="cl-card"><b>Empty regional partition</b><span>No example orders homed here</span></div><span class="cl-small">Empty does not mean this region has no replicas of other partitions.</span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="cl-banner">SQL identity stays order_id: 103 is one order across the database.</div>
  </div>
  <p class="cl-caption">An independent copy of the three shop orders, after purchase 103. These are logical home partitions and readable index-key prefixes, not three physical ranges or exclusive storage locations. The added history index orders by customer, descending time and descending order ID; dates abbreviate the original UTC timestamps. Every partition’s ranges are replicated.</p>
</figure>
